# What the kafka form, booted as it ships, without a shell and without a
# config, must say on its console (make check-shellfree-kafka; test/boot;
# forms/demo/test/console has the format). Given no certificate, Kafka
# parks before kafka-setup writes or formats anything, and says why. make
# check-kafka boots it with its config, and checks what it refuses.

seen    kafka-needs-config  leash: \{"event":"down","service":"kafka","why":"config tls-cert: FileNotFound"\}
unseen  setup-ran           kafka-setup:
